# Planted bugs for the checked design. Each one must make its property fail.
run fv-tlc DagScheduler.tla Checked.cfg WitnessBothDone.cfg
properties NeverRunsTwice NeverRunsOnPartialUpstream EventuallyBothDone
file DagScheduler.tla

mutation a checked restart resumes running without reading the effect count
detects NeverRunsTwice
-     /\ statusA' = IF effectA > 0 THEN "executed" ELSE "running"
+     /\ statusA' = "running"

mutation B treats a merely started A as good enough, even when checked
detects NeverRunsOnPartialUpstream
- ADependencyMet == IF Order = "checked" THEN statusA = "done" ELSE statusA # "pending"
+ ADependencyMet == statusA # "pending"

mutation marking A done stays possible but nothing ever requires it to happen
detects EventuallyBothDone
- Work == MarkRunningA \/ ExecuteA \/ MarkDoneA \/ RestartNaive \/ RestartChecked \/ RunB
- Next == Work \/ Crash \/ Done
+ Work == MarkRunningA \/ ExecuteA \/ RestartNaive \/ RestartChecked \/ RunB
+ Next == Work \/ Crash \/ MarkDoneA \/ Done

harmless a comment on the restart action
- \* Source: scheduler.on_restart(a), which checks the durable effect count
+ \* Source: scheduler.on_restart(a). It checks the durable effect count
